{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"636019335231569940","content":"“Memory says more about who we are than who we were. It shapes us as we shape it. Only our senses inform it.” Fabertell casts minor illusion to illustrate what they are saying depicting a memory. “What senses do we not have, what memories are we not forming, what makes us think it is complete when it is fractional.”","created_at":"2020-07-26T00:17:12.461000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"736738861220364299","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
